      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Jack London State Historic Park preserves the ruins of Wolf House, ranch buildings, the London graves, and a museum in Charmian’s House of Happy Walls.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glen_Ellen%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1,400‑acre park features historic structures, orchards, a lake, and a 19th‑century winery that still operates today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.sonoma.com/explore/glen-ellen/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Sonoma Creek, the valley’s main river, winds through Glen Ellen, adding to its scenic charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
